WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
The refrigeration cycle is the foundation of everything you'll do in this trade.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
The compressor compresses low-pressure vapor into high-pressure gas. Residential
systems use scroll compressors (two spiral scrolls, one orbiting) and
reciprocating compressors (piston and cylinder). The motor has C, S, and R

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Scroll Compressor: Two interlocking spirals compress refrigerant. Quieter and
more efficient.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
C-S-R Terminals: Common, Start, Run terminals for winding resistance diagnosis.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Before condemning a compressor always check
the capacitor and contactor first. Those are much cheaper.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Humming compressor usually means bad capacitor not bad
compressor. And — Always check capacitor and contactor BEFORE condemning
compressor

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Before you move on — what happens to refrigerant in the evaporator? Don't look
it up. Think about it.

